config RT_DIAGNOSTICS
    bool "Bounded numerical runtime diagnostics"
    default n
    help
      Owner-thread numerical instrumentation with caller-supplied timestamps.
      No allocation, formatting, timers or worker threads. Fixed-size caller-owned
      state; updates do bounded integer arithmetic. Snapshots copy the whole
      layout and reset only a window. Disabling creates no-op inline updates;
      arguments still follow normal C evaluation. Does not measure power.

config RT_DIAGNOSTICS_DETAILED_TIMING
    bool "Stage and interval measurements"
    depends on RT_DIAGNOSTICS
    default y
    help
      Disable to compile stage/interval record operations into no-ops. The fixed
      snapshot layout remains unchanged for ABI consistency; cycle/event counts
      still work. Enabled recording adds bounded arithmetic per measured stage,
      not a timer or task. Timestamps must share the owner clock.
